    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MMWard Estate Agents are delighted to present No. 16D Garden Apartment to the market. \nThis spacious ground-floor apartment is ideally positioned within this popular and well-maintained development, offering well-proportioned accommodation, an exceptional range of built-in storage throughout, two designated parking spaces and access to a communal rear garden.\n\n\nThe property is approached through a gated entrance and benefits from two designated parking spaces.\n\nPresented in great condition throughout, the apartment features double-glazed windows, recessed ceiling lighting in the living area and an impressive range of bespoke built-in units, providing excellent storage while maximising the available space.\n\n\nOn entering the apartment, the hallway features attractive wooden flooring, a large wall mirror, stylish wall-effect tiling and an enclosed storage cupboard.\n\nThe bright and spacious open-plan living and kitchen area forms the heart of the home. \nThe living area features a combination of wooden and tiled flooring, recessed ceiling lighting and extensive built-in storage on both sides. A patio door provides direct access to the communal rear garden, creating a natural extension of the living space.\n\nThe modern fitted kitchen offers ample storage and features an attractive polished concrete-effect splashback.\n It is equipped with an oven, hob, extractor fan, integrated dishwasher and fridge freezer, while a window allows plenty of natural light to fill the space.\n\nThe apartment offers two well-proportioned bedrooms, both featuring wooden flooring and built-in wardrobes, providing excellent storage. \n\nThe main bathroom is finished with tiled walls and wooden flooring and features a distinctive wood-panelled, lowered Jacuzzi bath, together with a window, WC, wash hand basin, bidet and additional built-in storage.\n\nA particular feature of this apartment is the extensive range of high-quality built-in units throughout, providing exceptional storage and helping to maximise the use of space while maintaining a clean and uncluttered finish.\n\nAdditional features include a water pressure booster pump, ensuring consistent water pressure throughout the apartment, and an air extraction system which removes air from the bathrooms to the outside.\n\nThe annual management fee is approximately 1,200.\n\nLocation\n\nNo. 16D Garden Apartment enjoys a convenient location in Naas, a thriving market town in County Kildare, renowned for its excellent range of amenities and vibrant town centre. \nNaas offers an extensive selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants and bars, together with a choice of primary and secondary schools.\n\n\nThe area also benefits from excellent recreational facilities, including Monread Park, K Leisure, Naas Golf Club and Naas Racecourse, catering for a wide range of sporting and leisure interests.\nThe property is ideally positioned for commuters, with easy access to the N7 and M7 motorway networks, providing convenient connections to Dublin and surrounding areas. Sallins railway station is also within easy reach and offers regular rail services to Dublin Heuston and other destinations, with a feeder bus service connecting the station with Naas town centre.\n\n\nNo. 16D Garden Apartment offers an excellent opportunity for a first-time buyer, downsizer or investor seeking a spacious and well-appointed apartment in a convenient Naas location. With its generous accommodation, exceptional built-in storage, two designated parking spaces and access to communal gardens, this property is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers.\n\n\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the accommodation, presentation, excellent storage and convenient location this property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\nWooden flooring, large wall mirror wall-effect tiling and an enclosed storage cupboard providing excellent additional storage.\n\nOpen plan living/ kitchen - 14'3\" (4.34m) x 31'5\" (9.58m)\nThe kitchen features part-tiled and part-wood flooring, with a modern fitted kitchen offering plenty of storage and an attractive polished concrete-effect splashback.\n The kitchen is equipped with an oven, hob, extractor fan, integrated dishwasher and fridge freezer, with a window providing natural light.\n\nThe living area benefits from enclosed storage on both sides and a patio door providing direct access to the communal rear garden.\n\nBathroom\nWooden flooring, tiled walls and a wood-panelled lowered Jacuzzi bath. The bathroom also features a window, WC, bidet, wash hand basin and built-in storage.\n\nBedroom 1 - 10'2\" (3.1m) x 12'0\" (3.66m)\nWooden flooring, a window and two built-in storage units providing excellent storage.\n\nBedroom 2 - 9'6\" (2.9m) x 12'8\" (3.86m)\nWooden flooring and built-in wardrobe providing excellent storage.\n\nEnsuite\nWooden floors, tiled and polished wall effect, wc, whb, walk in shower with glass door\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
